WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Straight from her US tour, please welcome Aurora!

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.860
Welcome.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.820
Welcome here!

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:15.860
Thanks!

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.600
Aurora, you've arrived

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.780
from the US now.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.420
Yes.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.820
Do you feel, when you're standing there

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.160
that you've got your dream job?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.480
No.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.600
You don't?

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.960
No.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.060
I think it's very rewarding there and then.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.640
Because I get a nice

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.780
contact with real people.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.640
And I get the opportunity to see people.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.400
Which gives me hope for mankind.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.760
It's very beautiful because they open up.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.120
So I get to see the most beautiful part of people.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.780
When I play for them.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.140
It's very beautiful.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.520
But afterwards I'm just ...

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.840
I'm finished.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.760
I'm finished. Or

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.780
I feel like I'm doing what I'm supposed to do when I create music.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.640
Then I feel like I know why I was born.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.060
But not when I'm on stage.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.540
Wow.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.120
Awesome.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.520
Then you just have to pass it on, but ...

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.160
Yes. It feels more like ...

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.760
When I'm in the studio creating music, I'm the mother, the father

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:27.960
and the child.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.880
I'm everyone.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.480
I'm the entire world. And God.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.480
When I create and decide.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.560
It's wonderful.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.140
And it's a feeling I can't describe.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.900
The feeling you have afterwards.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.660
When you've made something that's yours.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.080
Which no one can take away from you.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.680
I love that more than anything on this earth.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.800
But being on stage, I feel more like

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.640
maybe a

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.180
a tool.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.680
Or something that it just passes through.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.520
Just as if I had a hole in my head.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.580
And it comes from somewhere else.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.120
And goes out though the mouth, or the hands!

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.640
You're pretty concerned with how things

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.440
feel and what they sound like.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.700
You're going to play for us later.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.560
Yes!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.980
And I was watching your sound check.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.800
And I saw you walking around touching the edge of the stage.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.040
And you touched some of the lights.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.140
Yes.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.200
I think it's ... I get ...

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.040
I really want to touch things.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.580
I really want to touch the carpet here, now.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.380
Feel free, go for it!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.380
But. I'm really curious to know if things are warm.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.040
You can watch something and you wonder:

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.060
Is it warm? Is it cold? Is it ..?

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.080
It's very pleasing to touch things.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.980
And get to know ...

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.880
I often touch people without them knowing!

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.940
When I'm in a queue.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.660
Or at the airport!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.960
Just quickly.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.060
On the jacket, or ...

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.360
I try not to, but it's difficult.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.220
I mentioned earlier, you're not very fond of listening to music?

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.120
No.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.460
Do you have any Eurovision favourite?

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.880
Uhmmm.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.140
«Too Late For Love»!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.200
«Too Late For Love»!

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.140
«Too Late For Love»!

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.280
The whole of Norway will be upset with you!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.420
Last time we spoke together was in 2016.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.480
That year was some sort of breakthrough year for you.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:56.440
And a pretty chaotic year.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.720
If I understand correctly.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.920
Yes. I thought it was a difficult year.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.480
Musically, I was a little ...

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.200
I hadn't learned that everything can't be completely perfect.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.660
And I really struggled with that.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.900
I've learned now! Now I can release music without becoming completely depressed.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.980
But I couldn't do that then.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.480
We said yes to too many things, we had over 200

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.520
performances.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.160
In one year?

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.180
In one year.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.580
And then ...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.540
I was sick a lot of the time, and I lost my voice.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.040
And I ended up in the hospital.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.640
And I had to cancel my last three shows in the US, in December.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.460
Because I had to remove my appendix.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.560
And I didn't understand what that English word meant.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.800
«We have to remove your appendix, miss.»

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.600
And I didn't understand!

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.380
You just knew that they were going to remove something, but you didn't know what?!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.980
No, I didn't really understand what it meant in Norwegian!

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.020
And I called home.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.200
And it was 4 a.m. at home.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.280
My mom said: «It'll be okay, it's your appendix.»

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.820
«They will induce narcosis.»

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.860
And i was in a lot of pain, so I thought it was quite okay.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.460
And they listened to my music while they were performing the surgery!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.740
Wow!

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.320
Because they had to put a tube down my throat, right.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:15.620
And I said: «I'm a singer, please be careful with my throat!»

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.600
She said: «Yes, of course!»

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.180
And she was very careful.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.780
And they listened to my music while they were performing the surgery!

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.840
I was laying naked on the table.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.440
And I was cut up.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.320
Imagine, they've been inside me!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.480
Simultaneously as they've been inside my soul!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.900
I think it's fantastic to think about!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.280
One has never thought about it like that.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.200
But as you say it ...

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.060
It's very beautiful! It's very ...

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.600
I think organs are very beautiful.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.340
As you will see in my next album.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.760
What it looks like inside.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.480
I very much love organs and think it's very nice.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.260
I asked if I could bring it back home.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:55.880
What?

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.040
The appendix!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.740
To bring your appendix back home?

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.500
I wasn't allowed to.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.900
It's probably illegal to take it over the continent.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.180
That's fantastic!

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.960
You've worked very closely with

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:11.140
your family. And with your sisters, in particular.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.600
And one thing was that they were worried about you, but

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.120
you have a sister named Viktoria.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.080
Who is bipolar.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.040
Yes.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:28.540
What kind of support have you been able to give her?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.300
Because then you've had another role, as a next of kin.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.400
We are three sisters.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.460
And we all have our vulnerabilities and strangenesses.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.780
So when I was little, I didn't notice anything special about Viktoria.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.640
Or, of course, special as in that she's fantastic, but ...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:51.300
Nothing that was heavy in my life.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.880
And we're very good for each other, and we've always had a very special bond.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.320
And I think the most important thing I learned

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.980
as a human being and as a sister, and that I hope everyone else

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.280
close to someone with a mental disease can learn too, is that we ...

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.720
That when someone ...

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:19.180
When someone sends you anger and darkness or sorrow or tears, it's not ...

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.080
To know that it's not your fault.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.660
Because that will make life hard, I think.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.740
As long as you know it's not your fault

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.640
and it's not her fault. It's in a way a darkness

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.700
and a common enemy that both Viktoria and us as a family have together.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.040
Because we know that this is something she struggles with inside her.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.240
So I try to look at it like

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.800
it's something we stand together against. Even though she has to bear the brunt.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.300
But she's very strong!

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.060
Both my sisters are very strong.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.520
You're a person who carries sorrow for a long time.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.620
Are you carrying a sorrow?

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.400
I'm carrying many sorrows.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:55.940
Yes.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.020
I've lost quite a lot of people.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.240
And I carry a lot of the world's sorrows.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:06.360
I think it's difficult to ... That may be why I think it's difficult to meet a lot of people, because ...

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:12.640
You can sense quickly in people if they're going through something.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.800
Or if they ...

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.880
And there are insecurities. And people ... We can have such trouble putting words to our feelings.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.280
And it can be so painful.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.020
Everyone has something to struggle with.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.960
And that's also something I've learned.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.040
Especially from Viktoria.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.300
And Miranda. And myself!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.780
That we all have ...

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.480
Everyone should be a little excused in this life.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.840
Because we people have a lot ...

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.020
It's difficult being a human being today, it's an extreme sport in itself!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.340
But I do carry everything.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.740
And that may be why music is so important right now.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.360
Because it's a way to get it out.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.480
Your production is huge.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:55.640
You write a lot.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:01.100
And it's being said that you've written a whole album

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:04.300
that will be published after your death.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.060
It's very early to think about that, Aurora!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:07.900
Yes!

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:12.060
I've thought a lot about death in my life.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.600
I think about it a lot, but not in a bad way.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.000
Not with fear.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.980
But with a form of curiosity.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:21.920
I think it's interesting that we're all going to die.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.940
And that we manage to live without thinking about it constantly.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:28.860
And that some of us can't handle it and that we ...

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.880
... love each other so much knowing that we may lose each other.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.060
I think it's very beautiful.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.120
It makes life, of course, very precious and all that.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.460
I thought a lot about death when I was little.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:42.640
I remember that when I got nice things for my birthday, I would get sad.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.820
Because I thought: «But I'm going to die one day!»

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.380
«What will I do with this thing then?!»

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:50.200
«Then I can't be with this teddy bear or ...»

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.740
I started very early.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:55.320
And that might be why I started to collect dead insects.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.940
Because that was a way to

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.000
a way to handle that.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.480
Because you keep it with you.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.200
And it's a beautiful thing. And you can see that

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.560
the body still exists a little while longer.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.860
Even thought the rest is moving on.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.440
And I write a lot about death in my music as well.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.880
But, yes, a life album!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.520
I'm making that now. Little by little.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.320
One song from every decade.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.400
So I've got two songs now.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.760
One from I was ten to twenty, and one ...

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.440
I've already written the song for this decade.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.720
But I'm looking forward to ... It'll be a little more fun to die!

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.380
Because ...

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.220
Because there will be ...

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:39.260
I can say something to the world afterwards.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.800
We hope that it will be at least a double album.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.680
Yes.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:49.980
And that it will take a long time to get to the publication of this record!

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:50.680
Yes!

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.440
Thank you so much for being here, we will get some more guests in.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.320
Thank you!

